# An int32 field that nobody meets empty takes four bytes, whatever int32 it holds: a cursor takes 32 bytes, not 48.
# The cell of a vertex gets smaller by its two int32s alone. Its references stay wide.
# An entry loses a third of its cell, so its count and its link have markers in four bytes. A task would lose a quarter: its slots stay wide.
# RUN(PLAN): plan layouts
# PLAN: layout L0 CompiledObject size=32
# PLAN: slot 0 "line" Int32 Inline
# PLAN: slot 1 "weight" OptionalDouble Inline
# PLAN: slot 2 "parent" OptionalCell32 Inline
# PLAN: layout L1 CompiledObject size=48
# PLAN: slot 0 "id" Int32 Inline
# PLAN: slot 1 "mark" Int32 Inline
# PLAN: slot 2 "first" JSValue Inline
# PLAN: slot 3 "second" JSValue Inline
# PLAN: slot 4 "third" JSValue Inline
# PLAN: layout L2 CompiledObject size=32
# PLAN: slot 0 "hash" Int32 Inline
# PLAN: slot 1 "count" OptionalInt32 Inline
# PLAN: slot 2 "next" OptionalCell32 Inline
# PLAN: slot 3 "key" {{*}}Cell32 Inline
# PLAN: layout L3 CompiledObject size=64
# PLAN: slot 0 "id" OptionalInt64 Inline
# PLAN: slot 3 "link" JSValue Inline
# PLAN: slot 4 "queue" JSValue Inline
